==English==

===Etymology===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*telh₂- (bear)}}
From {{der|en|la|collātum}}, past participle of {{m|la|cōnferō}}. Not related to [[collateral]].

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|en|/kɒˈleɪt/}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-collate.wav|Audio (Southern England)}}
* {{a|US}} {{IPA|en|/ˈkoʊ.leɪt/}}
* {{rhymes|en|eɪt}}
* {{hyphenation|en|col|late}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[examine]] [[diverse]] [[document]]s and so on, to [[discover]] [[similarity|similarities]] and [[difference]]s.
#: {{ux|en|The young attorneys were set the task of '''collating''' the contract submitted by the other side with the previous copy.}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=c. 1831|author=w:Samuel Taylor Coleridge|title=Notes on the Book of Common Prayer
|passage=I must '''collate''' it, word by word, with the original Hebrew.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[assemble]] something in a [[logical]] [[sequence]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1922|author=w:Virginia Woolf|title=[[w:Jacob's Room|Jacob’s Room]]|publisher=Vintage Classics|edition=paperback|page=101
|passage=Detest your own age. Build a better one. And to set that on foot read incredibly dull essays upon Marlowe to your friends. For which purpose one must '''collate''' editions in the British Museum.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=2021 September 22|author=John Potter tells Paul Stephen|title=Your guide to Europe|journal=RAIL|issue=940|page=65|text="Once '''collated''', all files are sent to an external printing business with a turnaround time of about seven days, and then most of the distribution is done in-house.}}
<!--Semantic relations: There is a sense of the verb "[[redact]]" that is synonymous with this sense of the verb "[[collate]]", but its currency is tenuous outside of the legal profession; it is marked as "obsolete" at Wiktionary's entry as of this comment's writing.-->
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[sort]] multiple copies of [[printed]] documents into sequences of individual [[page]] [[order]], one sequence for each [[copy]], especially before [[binding]].
#: {{ux|en|'''Collating''' was still necessary because they had to insert foldout sheets and index tabs into the documents.}}
# {{lb|en|obsolete}} To [[bestow]] or [[confer]].
#* {{RQ:Taylor Clerus Domini|paragraph=4|page=23|passage=Becauſe thoſe hereticall Biſhops being depoſed and reduced into Lay-communion, could not therefore '''collate''' baptiſme for their want of holy Orders: {{...}}}}
# {{lb|en|transitive|Christianity}} To [[admit]] a [[cleric]] to a [[benefice]]; to [[present]] and [[institute]] in a [[benefice]], when the person presenting is both the [[patron]] and the [[ordinary]]; followed by ''to''.
#: {{rfex|en}}

